---
import Chart from "./Chart.astro";
import { layers } from "../../data/landing";
import chart from "../../assets/charts/architecture-local-dark.svg";
---

<section class="wrap section" id="how-it-works">
  <div class="section-head">
    <p class="eyebrow">How it works</p>
    <h2 class="title">One platform, from raw files to dashboards.</h2>
    <p class="lede">
      Data moves through three medallion layers, each owned by one tool. Dagster orchestrates every run; around that path
      sit the catalog, the query engine and, when you want them, governance and dashboards.
    </p>
  </div>
  <Chart
    src={chart}
    alt="OpenLakeForge architecture: Dagster orchestrates dlt, Floe and dbt-trino over Bronze, Silver and Gold Iceberg tables in object storage, queried by Trino and Superset and governed by OpenMetadata"
  />
  <div class="grid grid-3 layers">
    {layers.map(({ tag, label, tool, text }) => (
      <article class="card">
        <span class={`tag tag-${tag}`}>{label}</span>
        <p class="text">{text}</p>
        <code>{tool}</code>
      </article>
    ))}
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .layers { margin-top: var(--olf-space-5); }
  .card .text { font-size: var(--olf-text-body); color: var(--olf-text-primary); }
</style>
